Rule 1 (tensor where is boolean-like and broadcastable to x; out matches x shape)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= (ndim(v_3) = 0 ∨ (ndim(v_3) = ndim(v_1) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : (shape(v_3, i) = 1 ∨ shape(v_3, i) = shape(v_1, i)))) ∧ min(v_3) ≥ 0 ∧ max(v_3) ≤ 1 ∧ ndim(v_2) = ndim(v_1) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) = shape(v_1, i)
>>
Rule 2 (scalar boolean where avoids ambiguous tensor truth; out matches x shape)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : bool} |= if v_3 then (ndim(v_2) = ndim(v_1) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) = shape(v_1, i)) else (ndim(v_2) = ndim(v_1) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) = shape(v_1, i))
>>
Rule 3 (tuple out must be length 1; tensor where is boolean-like and broadcastable to x)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tuple(tensor), v_3 : tensor} |= v_2.len = 1 ∧ (ndim(v_3) = 0 ∨ (ndim(v_3) = ndim(v_1) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : (shape(v_3, i) = 1 ∨ shape(v_3, i) = shape(v_1, i)))) ∧ min(v_3) ≥ 0 ∧ max(v_3) ≤ 1
>>
Rule 4 (suppress ambiguous boolean: tensor `where` must be scalar; also enforce `out` shape/dtype for out: tensor)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= ndim(v_3) = 0 ∧ ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i) ∧ dtype_(v_2) = dtype_(v_1)
